Part A: O(4,2) light cone, Howe-Tan (2.20)
  a=-1 (Delta=-a=1, KO lambda=-a-2=-1) summand S^(a,-): A+- zero on n-m=[1], A-+ zero on n-m=[1]
  a=-2 (Delta=-a=2, KO lambda=-a-2=0) summand S^(a,+): A+- zero on n-m=[2], A-+ zero on n-m=[0]
  a=-3 (Delta=-a=3, KO lambda=-a-2=1) summand S^(a,-): A+- zero on n-m=[3], A-+ zero on n-m=[-1]
  KO I (3.6.1) minimal-rep K-types for (4,2): H^a(R^4)xH^b(R^2), b=a+1: [(0, 1), (1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4)] ...
  SO(4) type of H^a(R^4) = (a/2,a/2) [INFERENCE]: every K-type has j1=j2

Part B: U(2,2) Siegel series, Lee-Loke (24)
  s=-1, sigma=1: c_x=0, c_y=-1
    R_a(0,1): (2.5,2.5;E=-6) (2,2;E=-5) (1.5,1.5;E=-4) (1,1;E=-3) (0.5,0.5;E=-2) (0,0;E=-1)
    R_a(0,2): (0,0;E=-11) (0.5,0.5;E=-10) (0,0;E=-9) (1,1;E=-9) (0.5,0.5;E=-8) (1.5,1.5;E=-8)
    R_a(1,0): (0,0;E=1) (0.5,0.5;E=2) (1,1;E=3) (1.5,1.5;E=4) (2,2;E=5)
    R_a(1,1): (3,3;E=-5) (2.5,2.5;E=-4) (3.5,3.5;E=-4) (2,2;E=-3) (3,3;E=-3) (4,4;E=-3)
    R_a(2,0): (0,0;E=3) (0.5,0.5;E=4) (0,0;E=5) (1,1;E=5) (0.5,0.5;E=6) (1.5,1.5;E=6)
  s=0, sigma=0: c_x=-1, c_y=-1
    R_a(0,2): (0,0;E=-10) (0.5,0.5;E=-9) (0,0;E=-8) (1,1;E=-8) (0.5,0.5;E=-7) (1.5,1.5;E=-7)
    R_a(1,1): (2.5,2.5;E=-5) (2,2;E=-4) (3,3;E=-4) (1.5,1.5;E=-3) (2.5,2.5;E=-3) (3.5,3.5;E=-3)
    R_a(2,0): (0,0;E=2) (0.5,0.5;E=3) (0,0;E=4) (1,1;E=4) (0.5,0.5;E=5) (1.5,1.5;E=5)
  => every K-type of I_2(s,sigma) has j1=j2 (Lee-Loke 3.3); a helicity-h ladder
     has lowest K-type (0,|h|) or (|h|,0) (Fernando-Gunaydin 6.26-6.29), so h!=0
     ladders cannot be subquotients of this scalar-character family.
